# MCP Architecture Spec: {{ spec_name }}

## Context

- slug: mcp-architecture
- owner: <role:person>
- approver: <role:person>
- produced_at: <YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ>
- use case: <data and tools exposed; from product>
- hosts: <Claude Desktop / VS Code / custom SDK app; from host catalogue>

## Protocol version (rule r1)

- protocol_version: `<protocol_version>` (YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2025-11-25)
- negotiation: server advertises this version in `initialize`; client rejects on mismatch
- upgrade plan: <who re-pins, trigger, test gate>

## Primitives (rule r2)

Tools = actions (mutate, compute). Resources = read-only data. Prompts = templates.

| Type | Name | Purpose | Side effects |
|---|---|---|---|
| tool | {{ tools }} | <what it does> | {{ mutates_computes }} |
| resource | {{ resources }} | <URI prefix and data served> | none |
| prompt | {{ prompts }} | {{ template_intent }} | none |

Misclassification check: <any resource that writes, any tool that only reads>

## Transport (rule r3)

- transport: `<transport>` (stdio / http_sse / streamable_http)
- scope: {{ scope }}
- rationale: <stdio for local desktop hosts; HTTP for remote or multi-tenant>
- decision-tree path: <branch taken in content/06-decision-tree.xml>

## Auth (rule r4)

- auth_method: `<auth_method>` (none_local / oauth2.1_pkce / api_key)
- rule: stdio -> none_local; any remote transport -> oauth2.1_pkce
- authorization server: {{ authorization_server }}
- scopes: {{ scopes }}
- api_key justification (if used): <why PKCE is not possible; approver sign-off>

## Tool description policy (rule r5)

- descriptions are plain statements of behaviour, no instructions to the model
- host renders descriptions in a distinguishable surface, never inlined into the system prompt
- review owner: <role:person>

## Capability attestation (rule r6)

- declared capabilities: <tools / resources / prompts / logging; exactly what the server registers>
- undeclared methods: rejected by the client with {{ undeclared_methods }}
- manifest or identity: <signed manifest / pinned cert / n/a for stdio>

